sec.p:
Secondary outcomes include:
Total consumption of analgesics within the first 24 postoperative hours (morphine milligram equivalents);
Preoperative and 24-h postoperative PPT (kPa) measured based on standardized algometry;
Cerebral functional status at baseline and 24-h postoperatively monitored through multiparametric electroencephalographic (EEG) analysis;
PSQI and HADS scores preoperatively and 24-h postoperatively;
Intraoperative administration of anesthetic agents, including total propofol consumption (mg/kg/h), cumulative remifentanil dosage (µg/kg/min), and neuromuscular blockade adequacy (train-of-four ratio ≥ 0.9);
Intraoperative nociceptive threshold, including continuous PTI trajectories (range 0–100), PTI variance in the presence of surgical stimuli (incision/retraction/closure), and time-weighted average PTI < 50 (nociceptive overload threshold).
